=== 3. Verify the application health endpoint ===
$ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' http://localhost:3000/health
{"status":"ok"}
HTTP 200

=== baseline stats ===
$ curl -s http://localhost:3000/stats
{"conversions":0}
=== 4. Perform at least two successful conversions ===
$ curl -s "http://localhost:3000/convert?lbs=150"
{"lbs":150,"kg":68.039,"formula":"kg = lbs * 0.45359237"}
$ curl -s "http://localhost:3000/convert?lbs=0.1"
{"lbs":0.1,"kg":0.045,"formula":"kg = lbs * 0.45359237"}
=== also exercise error cases ===
$ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' "http://localhost:3000/convert?lbs=0"
{"lbs":0,"kg":0,"formula":"kg = lbs * 0.45359237"}
HTTP 200

$ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' "http://localhost:3000/convert"
{"error":"Missing required query parameter: lbs"}
HTTP 400

$ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' "http://localhost:3000/convert?lbs=abc"
{"error":"lbs must be a number"}
HTTP 400

$ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' "http://localhost:3000/convert?lbs=-5"
{"error":"lbs must be a finite, non-negative number"}
HTTP 422

=== 5. Verify /stats reports the expected count ===
$ curl -s http://localhost:3000/stats
{"conversions":3}
=== 6. Automated test run (npm test) ===
$ cd app && BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000 npm test; cd ..

> lbs-to-kg-service@1.0.0 test
> node test/run-tests.js

