=== 8. Failure scenario: Redis becomes unreachable ===
$ docker compose stop redis
 Container 554project-redis-1  Stopping
 Container 554project-redis-1  Stopped

$ time curl -s -w "
HTTP %{http_code}
" --max-time 10 "http://localhost:3000/convert?lbs=10"
{"error":"Storage unavailable, please retry"}
HTTP 503
curl -s -w '\nHTTP %{http_code}\n' --max-time 10   0.00s user 0.01s system 44% cpu 0.025 total

=== app did not crash while redis was down ===
$ docker compose ps app
NAME               IMAGE                 COMMAND                  SERVICE   CREATED          STATUS                    PORTS
554project-app-1   lbs-to-kg-app:1.0.0   "docker-entrypoint.s…"   app       39 seconds ago   Up 33 seconds (healthy)   0.0.0.0:3000->3000/tcp

=== restarting redis, confirming automatic reconnection ===
$ docker compose start redis
 Container 554project-redis-1  Starting
 Container 554project-redis-1  Started

$ docker compose logs app --tail 10
app-1  | [redis] client error: getaddrinfo ENOTFOUND redis
app-1  | [redis] reconnecting to redis:6379...
app-1  | [redis] client error: getaddrinfo ENOTFOUND redis
app-1  | [redis] reconnecting to redis:6379...
app-1  | [redis] client error: getaddrinfo ENOTFOUND redis
app-1  | [convert] failed to increment conversions counter: The client is offline
app-1  | [redis] reconnecting to redis:6379...
app-1  | [redis] client error: getaddrinfo ENOTFOUND redis
app-1  | [redis] reconnecting to redis:6379...
app-1  | [redis] connected to redis:6379

$ curl -s -w '
HTTP %{http_code}
' "http://localhost:3000/convert?lbs=10"
{"lbs":10,"kg":4.536,"formula":"kg = lbs * 0.45359237"}
HTTP 200

